      "text": "To solve this problem, we will use vector geometry to find the coordinates of points \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\) and then calculate the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\).\n\nFirst, we place the prism in a 3D coordinate system. Let the base \\(ABC\\) be in the \\(xy\\)-plane with \\(A = (0, 0, 0)\\), \\(B = (12, 0, 0)\\), and \\(C = (6, -6, 0)\\). The height of the prism is 16, so the points \\(D, E,\\) and \\(F\\) will be directly above these points:\n- \\(D = (6, -6, 16)\\)\n- \\(E = (0, -16, 16)\\)\n- \\(F = (12, -16, 16)\\)\n\nNext, we find the midpoints \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\) of edges \\(AC\\), \\(BC\\), and \\(DC\\) respectively:\n- \\(X\\) is the midpoint of \\(AC\\):\n  \\[\n  X = \\left(\\frac{0+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2}, \\frac{0+0}{2}\\right) = (3, -3, 0)\n  \\]\n- \\(Y\\) is the midpoint of \\(BC\\):\n  \\[\n  Y = \\left(\\frac{12+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2}, \\frac{0+0}{2}\\right) = (9, -3, 0)\n  \\]\n- \\(Z\\) is the midpoint of \\(DC\\):\n  \\[\n  Z = \\left(\\frac{6+12}{2}, \\frac{-6-6}{2}, \\frac{0+0}{2}\\right) = (9, -6, 0)\n  \\]\n\nNow, we calculate the distances between the points \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\) to find the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\). The distance formula in 3D is:\n\\[\nd = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2 + (z_2 - z_1)^2}\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate the distance \\(XY\\):\n\\[\nXY = \\sqrt{(9 - 3)^2 + (-3 - (-3))^2 + (0 - 0)^2} = \\sqrt{6^2 + 0^2 + 0^2} = \\sqrt{36} = 6\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate the distance \\(YZ\\):\n\\[\nYZ = \\sqrt{(9 - 9)^2 + (-6 - (-3))^2 + (0 - 0)^2} = \\sqrt{0^2 + (-3)^2 + 0^2} = \\sqrt{9} = 3\n\\]\n\nFinally, calculate the distance \\(ZX\\):\n\\[\nZX = \\sqrt{(3 - 9)^2 + (-3 - (-6))^2 + (0 - 0)^2} = \\sqrt{(-6)^2 + 3^2 + 0^2} = \\sqrt{36 + 9} = \\sqrt{45} = 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nThe perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is the sum of these distances:\n\\[\n\\text{Perimeter} = XY + YZ + ZX = 6 + 3 + 3\\sqrt{5}\n\\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6 + 3\\sqrt{5}}\n\\]",
